WasmFS Node backend: open O_WRONLY write-only on the host

NodeState::open() opened the host's file with an fopen-style mode
string, and since Node's only write-only strings ("w", "a") truncate or
append, O_WRONLY opened it read-write ("r+"). The host refuses that for
a file that may be written but not read, so an existing write-only
(0200) file couldn't be opened for writing. _wasmfs_node_open() now
takes the access mode and passes the host's own O_RDONLY, O_WRONLY or
O_RDWR to fs.openSync().

Upstream: https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten/issues/27847 (open)
Draft: docs/upstream/emscripten-wasmfs-node-open-wronly.md

diff --git a/src/lib/libsigs.js b/src/lib/libsigs.js
